    <GaugingStation location="Dorchester Total" name="Frome" number="44004">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Combined station comprising of Loudsmill, Loudsmill Fish Pass and Stinsford.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Louds Mill has two Crump profile weirs of which the largest has broad crested abutments, crests 10.66m (side-spilling). Also a side Crump profile weir on Mill Stream 1.52m broad. A Larinier fish pass, situated adjacent to the main weir on the left bank, was completed in autumn 2008. Stage is measured and flow computed independently at Loudsmill Fish Pass. Gauging has shown that the stage discharge relationship for the Fish Pass is good. Bypassing very small. Rating includes side channel and is modular to 10cumecs. The third Crump profile weir at Stinsford (on the opposite side of the floodplain to Louds Mill), crest 3.04m wide, modular to 4.6 cumecs but potential for non-modularity due to weed growth downstream. At Stinsford the river inundates the floodplain as it is not in the valley bottom, and there is potential for significant flow on the floodplain to bypass both gauges. The three sites are combined to produce a total flow record called Dorchester Total. Protected flows combining Louds Mill and Stinsford gauges. Bypassing through the floodplain between the 2 sites is significant. No rating shown on NRFA as it is a combined site.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Combined station (Loudsmill, Loudsmill Fish Pass, Stinsford) consisting of 3 crump weirs and a Larinier fish pass.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Flows exist prior to October 1971 for Louds Mill only. Poor site, not rated at high flows. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Minor gw abstractions in catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk, with Upper Greensand and Gault, Lias and Oolites in headwaters. Land use is rural. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">G</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Confident in QMED flow estimates." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Significant bypassing between sites." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
